<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman; " ALIGN="left">Our equity real estate investments focus on a range of asset types with a focus on stabilized,
income-generating properties. These may include multifamily, industrial, net lease, retail and office assets, as well as other asset types, including, without limitation, healthcare, student housing, single family residential, senior living, data
centers, manufactured housing, hotel and storage properties. To a lesser extent, we will also invest in real estate value creation opportunities that incorporate property refurbishment, redevelopment and development, which we expect to own long-term
for both income generation and potential capital appreciation. While we expect our real estate investments will focus primarily on properties located in the United States, we intend to invest to a lesser extent in properties located in Canada,
Europe and the Asia-Pacific region and potentially other international markets. We currently seek to build a property portfolio comprised of approximately 75% stabilized, income-generating properties and 25% refurbishment, redevelopment and
development properties. We do not expect our property portfolio will consist of more than 10% of assets located outside of the United&nbsp;States. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">We expect to invest in the property types that are helped by the manner in which the COVID-19 pandemic has accelerated fundamental changes in
the way Americans use real estate to consume, work and live. We call this investment approach &#147;Enhanced Core.&#148; This forward-looking approach currently leads us to focus on last-mile warehouses, logistics terminals, industrial outdoor
storage and other granular, irreplaceable components of the logistics chain. We also are targeting efficient offices in distributed innovation markets where highly educated in-migrants from other parts of the United States are relocating for
high-quality jobs, short commutes and affordable housing. Our &#147;Enhanced Core&#148; approach also currently includes biotech lab space, healthcare centers, newly-built single family rental housing and affordable multifamily properties. We will
consider other property types as well when the Adviser&#146;s research demonstrates they will benefit from the new American economy. For example, as services once again grow as a share of consumption, we expect to see opportunities in
&#147;last-mile&#148; services delivery, which includes restaurants, veterinary facilities, educational centers and low-acuity healthcare properties. We may also consider reducing our allocations to some of the above-mentioned property types if the
Adviser&#146;s research shows their expected future returns have become less compelling. Importantly, &#147;Enhanced Core&#148; is a research-driven approach that may lead to changing property type targets as the economy and real estate markets
evolve. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-left:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">See &#147;Investment Objectives and Strategies&#148; for a more detailed discussion of the types of properties we intend to
