participation would potentially threaten our status as <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">a&nbsp;non-investment&nbsp;company</FONT> exempt from the Investment Company Act. This may prevent us from receiving an allocation with respect to certain
investment opportunities that are suitable for both us and one or more Other J.P. Morgan Accounts. We expect that no less than 55% of our assets will consist of investments in real property, including any joint ventures that we control. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">Qualifying for an exemption from registration under the Investment Company Act will limit our ability to make certain investments. For example, these
